<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Referral to thoracic oncology: consultation within two weeks to review the screening CT, PET-CT and EBUS results with him and plan treatment. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, lung cancer monograph (2026); NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (2026) [S]</item><item>Work-up of the Lung-RADS 4X nodule without delay: FDG PET-CT and brain MRI with contrast this week, then endobronchial ultrasound with systematic sampling of mediastinal and hilar nodes (at least stations 4R, 4L and 7, and any PET-avid node), with enough tissue for PD-L1 and comprehensive next-generation sequencing (EGFR, ALK, ROS1, BRAF, KRAS, MET exon 14, RET, NTRK, HER2) and plasma testing in parallel; nurse navigator to track each date. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Non-Small Cell Lung Cancer (2026); US Preventive Services Task Force. Screening for Lung Cancer: US Preventive Services Task Force Recommendation Statement. JAMA 2021;325(10):962-970 (PMID 33687470) (2021); Mazzone PJ, et al. Screening for Lung Cancer: CHEST Guideline and Expert Panel Report. Chest 2021;160(5):e427-e494 (PMID 34270968) (2021); Lung CT Screening Reporting and Data System (Lung-RADS) v2022 (2022); Silvestri GA, et al. Methods for staging non-small cell lung cancer: Diagnosis and management of lung cancer, 3rd ed: ACCP evidence-based clinical practice guidelines. Chest 2013;143(5 Suppl):e211S-e250S (PMID 23649440) (2013) [S]</item><item>Tobacco treatment at every visit: brief advice, varenicline offered with a quit date, the Arizona quitline and counseling; stopping smoking improves outcomes even after a lung cancer diagnosis. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, lung cancer monograph (2026); Tobacco Smoking Cessation in Adults, Including Pregnant Persons: Interventions (2021) [S]</item><item>Equity safeguards: a nurse navigator, written results and next steps at each visit, transport and cost help offered, and time from scan to treatment tracked against the goal. Guideline: Aldrich MC, et al. Evaluation of USPSTF Lung Cancer Screening Guidelines Among African American Adult Smokers. JAMA Oncol 2019;5(9):1318-1324 (PMID 31246249) (2019); Bach PB, et al. Racial differences in the treatment of early-stage lung cancer. N Engl J Med 1999;341(16):1198-1205 (PMID 10519898) (1999) [S]</item><item>Distress and depression screening at each visit, plain information he can share, and advance care planning when he is ready. Guideline: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, lung cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
</component>
